From 2a2e0292f9470e9fa9136adcadedae20821fea82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 04:51:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] core-update pause: a continuation yields before its
 first step boundary (t_01a1d31bf400d56c)

hermes-hub 2026-11-13: the instant drainer released a pause without an apply, the paused Desktop turns were
continued in place (kind=auto_continue) and asked to pause again, but a pause landed only at a step boundary:
a continuation reached its first one ~3 min after admission (setup incl. a 30 s pre_llm_call hook timeout, a
30 s first request, a 20 s tool). Its admission reservation stayed unpublished meanwhile, so every apply past the
60 s cap was refused and the next release re-admitted the turns into the next window.

A continuation re-runs a paused request, so until its first model request it has done nothing its next
continuation would not redo. The Desktop/TUI gateway now marks an auto_continue turn
(agent.update_pause_first_request) and such a turn:
- returns paused without starting (no request, nothing persisted) when the pause is already requested;
- pauses at its first iteration, before the first request (turn_iteration_prep._step_boundary_pause);
- lets the mid-tool cancel reach its first model request after the usual grace (model_request_can_yield),
  whose refunded iteration then pauses before any request.
Every other turn keeps waiting for a real step boundary.
